00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.040
I know I tried to.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.750
Let's get caught back up and then tomorrow
we're going to have some deeper dives into

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:20.380
some more, some more, some more deeper dives
into some particular elements, as I like to

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.710
call them, of what's going on with the virus.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.710
Our response?

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.710
The Democratic primary.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.710
So let's get right into it.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.880
Donald Trump has previously floated the idea
of being opened by Easter as a country, clearly

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.300
because medical experts have gotten to him.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.300
He has canceled that.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.780
Donald Trump announced yesterday during a
press briefing, which we covered live.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:44.110
It was outside the White House that we will
be closed until April 30, abiding by those

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.110
guidelines.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.860
The social distancing guidelines.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.390
And of course, this is sort of the case because
there are lots of states that are doing very

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.690
little so far.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:59.079
But for the states and the people who have
been distancing, closing nonessential businesses,

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:05.259
et cetera, it's going to be another 32 days
from today until we might be able to start

00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:06.850
opening things up.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:13.700
This is both depressing and frustrating, but
not surprising and clearly necessary.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.700
That's the reality.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.719
It's depressing and necessary in order to
continue fighting the virus.

00:01:18.719 --> 00:01:21.310
Here is Donald Trump yesterday announcing
this.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:27.779
The modeling estimates that the peak in death
rate is likely to hit in two weeks.

00:01:27.779 --> 00:01:30.810
So I'll say it again, the peak.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.329
The highest point of death rates.

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:38.049
Remember, this is likely to head into weeks.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:41.869
Nothing would be worse than declaring victory
before.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:46.990
The victory is one that would be the greatest
loss of all.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:54.810
Therefore, the next two weeks and during this
period is very important that every one strongly

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:59.869
follow the guidelines have to follow the guidelines
that are grade vise.

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:02.109
President holds up a lot.

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:03.399
He's holding that up a lot.

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:06.049
He believes in it so strongly.

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:13.400
The better you do, the faster this whole nightmare
will end.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:22.319
Therefore, we will be extending our guidelines
to April 30th to slow the spread.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.670
And Donald Trump is 100 percent correct.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.770
He's a liar.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.060
He's a bad president.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.060
He's incompetent.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.760
He cares more about his own ratings, as we
will talk about, than the death toll.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.480
But this is the right decision.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.549
And I'll talk to you a little bit about the
peak and the data.

00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:43.219
But when he said it, I simultaneously sort
of experience dread and relief.

00:02:43.219 --> 00:02:44.500
The numbers are exploding.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.840
The health care system is rapidly getting
closer and closer to being overwhelmed, which

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.760
increases the death rate, as we've tragically
seen in other countries, including Italy.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.140
And I'm struggling with it.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:00.770
I mean, my nature is to be out all the time,
to be in cafes, to be with friends, to be

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:01.930
at the gym, to be with family.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:02.930
I'm doing none of it.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.300
I've canceled multiple trips.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.610
A major show.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.010
Appearances may be getting canceled, but I've
got electricity.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.749
I'm not sick with the virus for the time being.

00:03:12.749 --> 00:03:15.170
And hopefully most of us won't be.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.930
We will be better off in the long run.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.129
And this is the right decision.

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:22.890
Now, as far as the numbers and the peak, there
is very good data.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:29.140
There's a model that every day is fine tuned
with the latest data from Dr. Christopher

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:35.129
Murray, professor of health metrics sciences,
medical doctor, professor.

00:03:35.129 --> 00:03:37.879
Really good study with confidence intervals
about this.

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:43.420
His estimate is that nationally, April 15th
will be the peak date.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:47.620
That means a 15 more days, 15 more full days
from today.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.260
Now, this is really, really important to understand
because some people here, April 15th, they

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.849
think great, that's when it's all wide open.

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:55.849
Others think, no, that can't possibly be.

00:03:55.849 --> 00:03:57.310
It seems too soon.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:04:00.989
The peak simply means we get to the top.

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:04.239
Not that we necessarily come down from it.

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:10.299
And the doctor expects that the peak will
last a few days, right around 20, 200 deaths

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:11.299
per day.

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:14.290
That's going to be a cluster of about six
days.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.299
April 14th tonight.

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:21.840
During those six days, he estimates somewhere
between twelve and 13000 people will die in

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.050
total and then it will start to decline.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:29.410
Twenty one hundred people will die then, you
know, two thousand and fifty.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:36.010
So if we are 15 days to the peak and the peak
will last five or six days, that means in

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:44.240
15 plus five plus another 15 days, meaning
35 more days, we'd be back to a day like today.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:49.600
If you consider the upswing and then the downswing,
we're roughly six to eight hundred people

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.600
will die.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.530
We're not sure yet of the exact numbers today.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:57.300
And in fact, the decline from the peak may
be more spread out at maybe a more gradual

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.319
decline than the asset.

00:04:59.319 --> 00:05:02.720
The peak, so this is with a confidence interval.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:07.840
So when you look at the graphic, you see the
dotted line, which says, for example, you

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.990
know, 20 271 deaths on April 15th.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.000
But it could be as few as eleven eighty that
day.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.080
It could be as many as thirty five hundred.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.610
That's the range with 22 71 being the number
in between.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.139
So that's what it's looking like now.

00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:27.490
And under this estimate, the total deaths
would be about 82000 in the U.S. for this

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.090
cycle of the virus.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.830
This is important to understand.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:36.349
This model doesn't look at the fact that these
pandemics will often have two or three peaks

00:05:36.349 --> 00:05:38.479
and the next one may come in the fall.

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:42.500
This is eighty two thousand deaths through
the end of the summer.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.970
Again, that's with a confidence interval.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:49.020
Could be as low as thirty nine thousand, could
be as high as one hundred forty two thousand

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.319
based on the data we have right now.

00:05:51.319 --> 00:05:56.970
The better we do with social distancing, the
lower the number is.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:00.379
And some day things will start to get back
to normal.

00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:01.530
But it's going to be months.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.710
And you know, somebody said to me over the
weekend, these things have a beginning, a

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.039
middle and an end.

00:06:07.039 --> 00:06:08.300
We are past the beginning.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.050
We are definitely in the middle of this right
now.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:18.569
Hopefully from mid April on, we'll start to
move from the middle to the end, at least

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:19.979
of phase one.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.819
And it's going to be a long fight.

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:24.699
All we can do is take it day by day.

00:06:24.699 --> 00:07:29.720
And that's what I'm trying

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:36.500
to do.

